Dear Managers,

A little more than an hour ago I asked:

>I am testing a HP SuperDLT, identified as COMPAQ  SDLT320, on a Tru64
>UNIX V4.0G system. vdump writes correctly to the tape, but when
>finished the tape is unloaded, and the log has a message
>
>unmapped scsi density code (0x49) - DDR entry needed
>
>The highest entry I can find in a /etc/ddr.dbase file is for a Tru64
>5.1 system:
>    scsi_tape_density[0x48] =   "131000_bpi"  131000     0
>
>Can anybody help with the corresponding entry for code 0x49 ?

and within minutes I had answers from
Fred N. van Kempen <fred@microwalt.nl>
Olle Eriksson <olle@cb.uu.se>
Johan Brusche <johan.brusche@hp.com>

Edit ddr.dbase as follows
scsi_density_table_size = 0x4a
scsi_tape_density[0x49] = "190000_bpi"       190000      0
then use ddr_config command to compile new /etc/dbase

which, needless to say, solved my problem immediately. Thanks to
everybody!

/Bjorn
