Hi all,

In summary, these attributes are no longer supported by the =
SNMPv2-capable agent in Tru64 5.x .

The following feedback to this question was received from HP:

"The 'missing' attributes are from the snmp subtree which is defined in =
RFC 1214.=20
The V4.0F os_mibs supported RFC's 1213, 1285, 1231 & 1514 (see the =
os_mibs manual page).=20
Note that although os_mibs implemented RFC 1214 it was not supported.=20
When the SNMPv2 support was added in Tru64 UNIX V5.0 the unsupported =
code implementing the SNMPv1 snmp subtree was removed and no new code =
was added to implement the SNMPv2 snmp subtree as defined by RFC 1907.=20
The V5.1B os_mibs implements and supports only RFC's 1213, 1231, 1285, =
1514, 2011, 2012, 2013 & 2358."

I do not have access to the Tru64 5.0 Release Notes to check whether =
these changes were mentioned anywhere.
At least as a Tru64 5.1B user, the documentation is not really =
sufficient to understand why these attributes, which are to my =
understanding actually defined in RFC1213, are no longer supported.

Best regards,
Michael




