Dear All,

I had some helpful comments from Martin Petder, but I dug around on the H=
P
website, and came up with:

    Models
   =20
    HP StorageWorks Network  Storage Router e1200
   =20
    262672-B21 MSL5000 EMBEDDED  FIBRE OPTION KIT =E2=80=93 GRAPHITE=20
   =20
    Includes one router card (1FC x 2 LVD SCSI), 2 VHDCI-VHDCI SCSI cable=
s,
    User Guide CD.  This SKU is for all MSL5000 Graphite colored librarie=
s.
    It is highly recommended that an  installation HP Care Pack be ordere=
d
    with this SKU.
   =20
    Benefits at a Glance
   =20
    Serverless Backup Support
    Customer selectable 2 Gb/1Gb Fibre Channel Support
    Web Based Management
    LVD SCSI Support
    Supports 2 Gb or 1Gb FC
    Provides connectivity for up to 2 tape drives per SCSI bus

Which was enough to reassure me, so I just wnt ahead and tried it, and
it works well.  The SCSI buses do indeed seem to be separate, as I have
the library and drives set up with the same SCSI IDs on both of them.=20
I now have 4 drives and 48 tape slots on my SAN, and visible to my ES40
and windows/linux machines.  Even better, the device files under Tru64
didn't change for the devices that were originally direct-attach SCSI.

Thanks again,

Andrew

