Here is a summary to the follow question:

I have been asked to compare the performance of two servers.  One is an ES4=
0 with 4 x 833MHz (EV6.8AL) CPUs and the other an 8400-5/625 with 8 x 613MH=
z (EV5.6) CPUs.  I have searched the archives and found some references to =
a Digital web site although it has since been removed.

Where can I find general Alpha CPU performance information?

Thanks go to:

Nasir Yilmaz (Sistem M=FCd=FCr Yardimcisi) [nyilmaz@iski.gov.tr]
Dr Thomas.Blinn@HP.com [tpb@doctor.zk3.dec.com]
Jim  Kurtenbach [KurtenbachJ@crlcorp.com]
Nikola Milutinovic [Nikola.Milutinovic@ev.co.yu]
Marc Schlensog [fishtank@d2mail.de]
A. Mahendra Rajah [Mahendra.Rajah@URegina.CA]
T. Horsnell (tsh) [tsh@mrc-lmb.cam.ac.uk]
Gergen, Peter [petergergen@kpmg.com.au]
Peter Reynolds [PJReynolds@Synstar.com]

and NO THANKS to the $30,000,000 bank transfer offer goes to:

snufA . Maryam [madamaba@indiatimes.com]

--------------------------------------------------------------

The general consensus was that the ES40 with its newer architecture should =
perform far better than the 8400.  This is also consistent with our observa=
tion.

Alpha System CPU performance figures are available at

http://h18002.www1.hp.com/alphaserver/performance/perf_by_name.html

This site was very helpful.  Some also pointed to

www.spec.org

although this did not provide the information I required.

